{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1061","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1061","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1061\",\"parent_revision\":\"d232bb1e17737a94e5a12ada902042cafd628e67\",\"root_revision\":\"1f94bebd131564e52fe18f5ecb40798d2a4553afac9d0cb4971530c5cb60121a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add effort level control (--effort flag) to kage-bunshin spawn and work-milestone dispatch\\nDate: 2026-04-12\\nGoal: Add --effort {low|medium|high|max} flag to kage-bunshin spawn.py and flow it through dispatch_spawn MCP tool, with effort tier guidance added to .claude/rules/model-selection.md.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all 9 conditions AVAILABLE\\n\\nThree implementation touch points (localized, no schema changes):\\n1. spawn.py: add --effort to p_spawn (~line 1082), add CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL injection to _build_spawn_shell_cmd (after line 585)\\n2. server.py: add effort param to _build_spawn_cmd signature + cmd construction (lines 4162/4178), add effort param to dispatch_spawn signature (line 4333) + thread to _build_spawn_cmd call\\n3. model-selection.md: append effort tier section after existing model table\\n4. test_spawn.py: add 3 test cases for the new flag\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add effort level control (--effort flag) to kage-bunshin spawn and work-milestone dispatch** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/claude-code-cli-power-patterns.md -- pattern: Opus 4.6 Effort Levels\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:15:06.133036Z</sub>\\n\\n- Goal: Add `--effort {low|medium|high|max}` flag to kage-bunshin `spawn.py`, expose it through the `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool in `server.py`, and add effort tier guidance to `.claude/rules/model-selection.md`.\\n- Status: APPROVED\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Functional intent: add `--effort` CLI flag to `spawn.py` and flow it through `dispatch_spawn` MCP tool; both are fully implemented.\\n  - Scope boundaries: three localized touch points (spawn.py, server.py, model-selection.md); no dispatch plan YAML schema changes required.\\n  - External interfaces: `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` env var injected before the `claude` binary in the child process shell command.\\n  - Existing system context: `--model` argument in spawn.py is the exact structural analog used as the implementation pattern; `EffortLevel` TypeAlias defined in server.py at line 63.\\n  - Verification expectations: three unit tests in test_spawn.py covering flag presence in help, env injection when set, and env omission when unset \u2014 all present and passing.\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Valid effort choices (`low`, `medium`, `high`, `max`) \u2014 derived from `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` accepted values; materialized as `EFFORT_LEVELS` constant at spawn.py line 89 and `EffortLevel` TypeAlias at server.py line 63.\\n- MISSING:\\n  - None \u2014 all conditions present at implementation time and verified against primary sources.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `spawn.py spawn --help` shows `--effort` flag with choices `{low,medium,high,max}`.\\n2. Spawning with `--effort low` results in the child process environment containing `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=low`.\\n3. `.claude/rules/model-selection.md` contains an effort tier section.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`kage-bunshin/scripts/spawn.py` accepts `--model` to select the model (haiku, sonnet, opus) but has no `--effort` flag to set `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` on the spawned `claude` process. The `work-milestone/SKILL.md` hardcodes `--model sonnet` in its spawn command template without any effort level parameter. The `model-selection.md` rule maps agents to models but does not mention effort tiers. All spawned sessions run at the default effort level regardless of task complexity.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:15:09.869621Z</sub>\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Feature\\n- Behavioral boundary: the spawned `claude` process environment \u2014 specifically whether `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` is injected, omitted, or rejected correctly based on the `--effort` argument passed to `spawn.py spawn` or the `effort` parameter of `dispatch_spawn`.\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: per-task effort tuning is observable in the child process environment via `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL`; cost and latency optimization is available to all callers of `dispatch_spawn` and direct `spawn.py` users.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`spawn.py` accepts `--effort {low|medium|high|max}` flag. When provided, the spawned `claude` process inherits `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL={value}` in its environment. `work-milestone/SKILL.md` dispatch plan schema includes an optional `effort` field per wave item. The `model-selection.md` rule includes effort tier guidance alongside model selection.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"534aceb86b7ebad8a41ae8182fb5873fdb3e916cd28ce3edd14d2bebbf9eb043\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPopaQw\"}"}